Database migrations (Alembic)
=============================

The schema is managed with Alembic. `migrations/env.py` reads the database URL
from `settings.DATABASE_URL`, so migrations target whatever database the app is
configured to use (SQLite in local dev, PostgreSQL in production).

Common commands (run from the `backend/` directory):

  # Apply all migrations (create/upgrade the schema)
  alembic upgrade head

  # Autogenerate a migration after changing app/models/models.py
  alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe your change"

  # Roll back the most recent migration
  alembic downgrade -1

Local development (SQLite)
--------------------------
`python init_db.py` creates the tables directly (via SQLAlchemy create_all) and
seeds the default admin, which is convenient for a fresh checkout. You can also
use `alembic upgrade head` to exercise the exact migration path.

Production (PostgreSQL)
-----------------------
1. Set DATABASE_URL, e.g.:
     DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg2://user:password@host:5432/workflowpro
2. Apply migrations:
     alembic upgrade head
3. Seed the admin user (respects ADMIN_EMAIL / ADMIN_PASSWORD; refuses the weak
   default password in production):
     python init_db.py

Always review autogenerated migrations before committing — Alembic cannot detect
every change (e.g. some server-default or enum edits) and may need hand-tuning.
